<article class="env-remark" id="09E8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09E8">Remark <span data-tag="09E8">15.113.6</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $K$. Let $L/K$ be a finite separable field extension. Let $B \subset L$ be the integral closure of $A$ in $L$. Picture: </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ B \ar[r] &  L \\  A \ar[u] \ar[r] &  K \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/032L" data-tag="032L">10.161.8</a> the ring extension $A \subset B$ is finite, hence $B$ is Noetherian. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00OK" data-tag="00OK">10.112.4</a> the dimension of $B$ is $1$, hence $B$ is a Dedekind domain, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/034X" data-tag="034X">10.120.17</a>. Let $\mathfrak m_1, \ldots , \mathfrak m_ n$ be the maximal ideals of $B$ (i.e., the primes lying over $\mathfrak m_ A$). We obtain extensions of discrete valuation rings </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A \subset B_{\mathfrak m_ i}  \]
</div>
  <p> and hence ramification indices $e_ i$ and residue degrees $f_ i$. We have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [L : K] = \sum \nolimits _{i = 1, \ldots , n} e_ i f_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02MJ" data-tag="02MJ">10.121.8</a> applied to a uniformizer in $A$. We observe that $n = 1$ if $A$ is henselian (by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04GH" data-tag="04GH">10.153.4</a>), e.g. if $A$ is complete. </p>
</article>